1
00:00:22,601 --> 00:00:26,671
Florence Dela Cruz, there's a letter for you.

2
00:00:26,671 --> 00:00:29,234
Is that the result
of your college admission test?

3
00:00:29,234 --> 00:00:30,869
- I got accepted!
- What?

4
00:00:30,869 --> 00:00:31,837
You got accepted!

5
00:00:31,837 --> 00:00:33,005
- Yes!
- My daughter got accepted!

6
00:00:33,005 --> 00:00:34,500
This is for Florence.

7
00:00:34,501 --> 00:00:37,171
- For Florence.
- For Florence!

8
00:00:37,171 --> 00:00:38,705
And this is for all of us.

9
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:41,641
- Yes, for all of us.
- Yes, for all of us!

10
00:00:42,543 --> 00:00:44,411
Federico?

11
00:00:44,411 --> 00:00:46,292
What happened?

12
00:00:48,449 --> 00:00:51,518
We still have money left.

13
00:00:51,518 --> 00:00:54,588
I also called your grandfather.

14
00:00:54,588 --> 00:00:56,824
He said he'll help us out.

15
00:00:56,824 --> 00:00:59,393
We can do this, Mother.

16
00:00:59,393 --> 00:01:01,862
We will fight, and we will win.

17
00:01:01,862 --> 00:01:03,397
I have a side hustle for you.

18
00:01:03,397 --> 00:01:04,665
Side hustle?

19
00:01:04,665 --> 00:01:07,868
All you have to do is cook delicious food.

20
00:01:07,868 --> 00:01:09,937
Now, cook me your best recipe.

21
00:01:09,937 --> 00:01:14,908
Prove to me that you can cook
for the grandchildren of Don Ferell.

22
00:01:16,112 --> 00:01:18,178
This is very good.

23
00:01:18,178 --> 00:01:20,681
It means you're hired, Ms. Florence.

24
00:01:20,681 --> 00:01:22,049
Really?

25
00:01:22,049 --> 00:01:24,356
Thank you, Sir!

26
00:01:24,356 --> 00:01:27,387
And I think it's better
if she meets the kids,

27
00:01:27,387 --> 00:01:30,891
because after all,
she'll be cooking for them.

28
00:01:30,891 --> 00:01:33,861
I'm sure that all your grandchildren
are so cute.

29
00:01:33,861 --> 00:01:35,662
You be the judge.

30
00:02:42,169 --> 00:02:44,604
Good thing that you're early.

31
00:02:45,398 --> 00:02:49,384
You can start doing lunch
for Don Ferell's grandsons.

32
00:02:49,384 --> 00:02:51,962
As you already know,
they are very picky eaters.

33
00:02:51,962 --> 00:02:56,009
That's why you have to ask them
what they want to eat

34
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:58,759
before you start cooking in the kitchen.

35
00:02:58,759 --> 00:03:01,916
You will receive half of your salary
every 15th,

36
00:03:01,916 --> 00:03:04,931
and, of course,
the other half is every end of the month.

37
00:03:04,931 --> 00:03:07,988
You will be provided for
with everything that you need,

38
00:03:07,988 --> 00:03:12,264
from soap, toothpaste, and shampoo,

39
00:03:12,264 --> 00:03:14,295
and among other thing else,

40
00:03:14,295 --> 00:03:17,866
like SSS, Philhealth, and Pag-Ibig.

41
00:03:17,866 --> 00:03:21,626
You only need to focus on one thing,
and one thing alone.

42
00:03:21,626 --> 00:03:24,805
Your job. And that is, to cook.

43
00:03:24,805 --> 00:03:26,506
And you'll be in charge in securing

44
00:03:26,506 --> 00:03:30,110
if you have enough kitchen supplies
from meats,

45
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:33,376
eggs, canned goods, seasoning, milk,

46
00:03:33,376 --> 00:03:40,853
and of course, included also are vegetables
and fruits, okay?

47
00:03:40,853 --> 00:03:43,790
Now, you have to be aware of what's lacking

48
00:03:43,790 --> 00:03:46,893
and what is needed to be changed.

49
00:03:46,893 --> 00:03:49,863
If you're not sure
if something is still fresh,

50
00:03:49,863 --> 00:03:52,799
then throw it away and don't regret it.

51
00:03:52,799 --> 00:03:53,924
What?

52
00:03:53,924 --> 00:03:56,436
But that's a pity,
a lot of people are hungry nowadays.

53
00:03:56,436 --> 00:03:58,171
So?

54
00:03:58,171 --> 00:04:00,508
The world can starve for all I care,

55
00:04:00,508 --> 00:04:02,443
but what's important is all the grandsons

56
00:04:02,443 --> 00:04:04,455
of Don Ferell will eat fresh food.

57
00:04:04,455 --> 00:04:09,377
That's why your kitchen must provide
whatever they ask for.

58
00:04:09,377 --> 00:04:12,002
Also, there are rules.

59
00:04:12,002 --> 00:04:16,029
They eat in their respective rooms
according to their own schedule

60
00:04:16,029 --> 00:04:18,541
and when they want to eat.

61
00:04:18,541 --> 00:04:22,651
That's why you have to be available for them

62
00:04:22,651 --> 00:04:25,424
anytime they need you to serve them.

63
00:04:25,424 --> 00:04:31,121
Now, the kitchen will be yours
and yours alone, Ms. Florence.

64
00:04:31,121 --> 00:04:34,425
All the responsibilities rest on you,

65
00:04:34,425 --> 00:04:38,662
so everybody in this household will eat,
understood?

66
00:04:39,296 --> 00:04:42,099
I'm very understanding, Ms. Serafica, so yes.

67
00:04:42,099 --> 00:04:44,234
I understood everything.

68
00:04:45,269 --> 00:04:46,670
Very good.

69
00:04:46,670 --> 00:04:48,368
Follow me.

70
00:04:49,218 --> 00:04:50,743
Walk this way.

71
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,857
Hurry.

72
00:05:08,626 --> 00:05:11,747
Everyone, this is Florence.

73
00:05:12,705 --> 00:05:14,465
Hi, Florence.

74
00:05:14,465 --> 00:05:16,807
I'm Patotina, maid number 2.

75
00:05:16,807 --> 00:05:19,003
Good luck.

76
00:05:19,003 --> 00:05:20,804
Hi. My name is James.

77
00:05:20,804 --> 00:05:23,160
Driver number 2. Good luck.

78
00:05:24,438 --> 00:05:27,471
Iking, Florence... Iking.

79
00:05:28,812 --> 00:05:31,048
Wait, aren't you the mailman?

80
00:05:31,048 --> 00:05:35,383
No, that's just my part-time job.

81
00:05:36,406 --> 00:05:41,458
But this is my main job, I'm gardener 1.

82
00:05:41,458 --> 00:05:44,367
And I'm sure you know Dencio.

83
00:05:48,153 --> 00:05:50,467
Well, I will leave you.

84
00:05:50,467 --> 00:05:51,976
Follow me.

85
00:05:58,375 --> 00:06:00,002
Walk this way.

86
00:06:01,634 --> 00:06:04,221
She said to follow her.

87
00:06:09,353 --> 00:06:11,937
This will be your room.

88
00:06:11,937 --> 00:06:15,426
And it will be your own personal space.

89
00:06:15,426 --> 00:06:17,775
Once you're done with all your work,

90
00:06:17,775 --> 00:06:21,231
you can retire here
and no one will bother you.

91
00:06:21,231 --> 00:06:25,035
As you can see,
I have provided you with your uniforms.

92
00:06:25,035 --> 00:06:28,713
We must always look professional.

93
00:06:28,713 --> 00:06:30,902
You will have access to wi-fi,

94
00:06:30,902 --> 00:06:37,948
and the password is
"Ferell brothers are super hot and awesome",

95
00:06:37,948 --> 00:06:41,719
with the capital letter F,
no space in between.

96
00:06:41,719 --> 00:06:45,389
Don't bother to ask,
the boys set that password.

97
00:06:45,389 --> 00:06:49,827
But if you'll ask me,
it will be Capital Letter I,

98
00:06:49,827 --> 00:06:54,241
small letters l, u, s, uppercase G-M-A,

99
00:06:54,241 --> 00:06:56,367
SHARPSEVEN number 1.

100
00:06:56,367 --> 00:06:58,406
No space in between.

101
00:06:58,406 --> 00:07:03,006
Oh, by the way, Ms. Florence,
I must warn you.

102
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:06,343
Don't thinks that just because
you're accepted, you're already secured.

103
00:07:06,343 --> 00:07:09,847
You can only make a mistake once
and after that,

104
00:07:09,847 --> 00:07:12,582
I will personally drag you out of here.

105
00:07:12,582 --> 00:07:16,442
I will not tolerate incompetence.

106
00:07:17,554 --> 00:07:21,142
So, settle down

107
00:07:21,142 --> 00:07:23,741
and proceed to meet the boys in the game room

108
00:07:23,741 --> 00:07:26,396
and ask them what they want to eat,

109
00:07:26,396 --> 00:07:28,632
and then start preparing their meals.

110
00:07:28,632 --> 00:07:30,968
- Clear?
- Yes.

111
00:07:30,968 --> 00:07:32,503
Okay.

112
00:07:32,503 --> 00:07:34,318
Good luck.

113
00:07:41,612 --> 00:07:43,573
Wow.

114
00:07:43,573 --> 00:07:46,070
This room is so grand.

115
00:07:46,850 --> 00:07:49,997
This is bigger than our house.

116
00:07:52,756 --> 00:07:57,261
Cabinets, kitchen, but here we go.

117
00:07:57,261 --> 00:07:58,758
Speaking of the kitchen,

118
00:07:58,758 --> 00:08:01,899
are you ready, Florence,
because if you're ready,

119
00:08:01,899 --> 00:08:07,404
give me an F, give me an L,
give me an O, R, E, N, C, E!

120
00:08:07,404 --> 00:08:11,108
I'm Florence Dela Cruz and I'm ready to cook!

121
00:08:11,108 --> 00:08:14,878
I can cook sinigang, pinakbet, adobo, tinola,

122
00:08:14,878 --> 00:08:18,482
nilaga, everything, Florence can do that.

123
00:08:18,482 --> 00:08:22,553
So for the heart, for you, dear hearts,

124
00:08:22,553 --> 00:08:24,888
for Mother and Father, let's go!

125
00:08:24,888 --> 00:08:27,390
Start! Let's go, Florence.

126
00:08:28,328 --> 00:08:29,526
Hi, Sir Aldus.

127
00:08:29,526 --> 00:08:32,563
What would you like to have for lunch today?

128
00:08:32,563 --> 00:08:34,431
I want sushi.

129
00:08:34,431 --> 00:08:37,868
But please make sure you slice it
thinly and properly.

130
00:08:37,868 --> 00:08:41,071
The same way how Chef Jiro does it.

131
00:08:41,071 --> 00:08:42,756
Do you know him?

132
00:08:42,756 --> 00:08:44,107
You better watch him,

133
00:08:44,107 --> 00:08:47,252
so you'd learn how to make sushi properly.

134
00:08:47,252 --> 00:08:49,418
Make sure the tuna is fresh.

135
00:08:49,418 --> 00:08:52,382
And freshly cut and I don't want it frozen.

136
00:08:52,382 --> 00:08:55,419
It should be as fresh as
the tunas in the Tsukiji market,

137
00:08:55,419 --> 00:08:58,088
something that would make me
feel that I'm in Japan.

138
00:08:58,088 --> 00:08:59,443
Get it?

139
00:09:00,182 --> 00:09:01,673
Move over.

140
00:09:05,229 --> 00:09:06,858
What are you waiting for?

141
00:09:10,969 --> 00:09:13,056
Sushi, coming up.

142
00:09:19,111 --> 00:09:22,800
Hello, Sir Troy,
what do you want for lunch today?

143
00:09:25,372 --> 00:09:27,946
Sir Troy, what would you like for lunch?

144
00:09:27,946 --> 00:09:29,860
Can't you see I'm playing?

145
00:09:30,812 --> 00:09:34,402
Sir Troy, I still need
to buy the ingredients.

146
00:09:34,402 --> 00:09:35,808
Destroy.

147
00:09:35,808 --> 00:09:37,374
It's your fault.

148
00:09:39,151 --> 00:09:41,085
I want a paella valenciana.

149
00:09:41,748 --> 00:09:42,900
Okay.

150
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:45,556
But please, don't put chorizo.

151
00:09:45,556 --> 00:09:47,588
No chorizo.

152
00:09:47,588 --> 00:09:48,935
Is that all?

153
00:09:48,935 --> 00:09:50,042
All right.

154
00:09:50,042 --> 00:09:53,812
But I also want something
like paella verduras,

155
00:09:53,812 --> 00:09:57,673
the one with red bell pepper,
zucchini, and tomatoes.

156
00:09:58,668 --> 00:10:00,005
Yeah.

157
00:10:01,336 --> 00:10:02,675
Is that it?

158
00:10:04,953 --> 00:10:09,226
But also make it like paella negra,

159
00:10:09,226 --> 00:10:11,055
and put some squid ink on it.

160
00:10:14,668 --> 00:10:16,262
Is that it?

161
00:10:19,272 --> 00:10:21,537
But not too much.

162
00:10:21,537 --> 00:10:24,031
It's not appetizing anymore if it's too dark.

163
00:10:26,132 --> 00:10:28,893
Not too dark.

164
00:10:28,893 --> 00:10:30,404
Is that all?

165
00:10:30,404 --> 00:10:32,129
Yeah.

166
00:10:32,129 --> 00:10:33,931
Are you sure?

167
00:10:36,248 --> 00:10:37,423
Yeah?

168
00:10:56,336 --> 00:10:59,068
Sir Tristan, what's your order?

169
00:11:01,968 --> 00:11:03,287
Sir?

170
00:11:05,731 --> 00:11:07,072
Sir?

171
00:11:08,363 --> 00:11:10,998
What's with you? I'm lifting weights.

172
00:11:11,858 --> 00:11:13,387
I'm sorry.

173
00:11:13,387 --> 00:11:16,381
I want an apple pie.

174
00:11:16,381 --> 00:11:17,970
Apple pie...

175
00:11:17,970 --> 00:11:21,329
No, no, lemon pie...

176
00:11:21,329 --> 00:11:24,944
- Lemon pie.
- No, I want mango pie...

177
00:11:25,757 --> 00:11:28,862
But I hope there's a layer of sugary crust,

178
00:11:28,862 --> 00:11:31,642
but it shouldn't be too crusty.

179
00:11:31,642 --> 00:11:34,678
Crusty, not crunchy.

180
00:11:34,678 --> 00:11:38,595
I don't want the sound of crunch
when I eat it.

181
00:11:38,595 --> 00:11:43,520
And please, I don't want just any mangoes.

182
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:47,308
I want Guimaras mangoes.

183
00:11:47,308 --> 00:11:51,518
The sweetest and the best mangoes
in the world.

184
00:11:52,713 --> 00:11:54,982
Mango pie, Sir, with Guimaras mangoes?

185
00:11:54,982 --> 00:11:56,219
Sure.

186
00:13:51,999 --> 00:13:54,419
- What's that?
- Sushi.

187
00:13:56,570 --> 00:13:57,909
What's this?

188
00:13:59,549 --> 00:14:02,694
I said I want to dream of sushi,

189
00:14:02,694 --> 00:14:05,813
but with what you did,
it's like I'll have a nightmare.

190
00:14:05,813 --> 00:14:07,870
I'm not going to eat that.

191
00:14:07,870 --> 00:14:10,617
That's an insult to Japanese culture,

192
00:14:10,617 --> 00:14:13,620
that's an insult to human civilization.

193
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:16,023
Take that out in front of me.

194
00:14:16,023 --> 00:14:17,336
Out!

195
00:14:33,503 --> 00:14:36,257
- What's that?
- Paella negra.

196
00:14:37,552 --> 00:14:41,113
Even a stray dog who hasn't eaten for months
won't eat that.

197
00:14:41,113 --> 00:14:43,016
And now you're asking me to eat it?

198
00:14:43,016 --> 00:14:44,588
Are you crazy?

199
00:14:45,304 --> 00:14:47,693
Or are you planning on making me sick?

200
00:15:14,882 --> 00:15:16,359
Nice one.

201
00:15:19,853 --> 00:15:21,321
Mango pie, Sir.

202
00:15:21,321 --> 00:15:25,174
I'm sorry I wasn't able
to find Guimaras mangoes.

203
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:28,819
What do you mean you can't find
Guimaras mangoes here in Levante?

204
00:15:30,310 --> 00:15:33,064
So you made a mango pie

205
00:15:33,064 --> 00:15:35,550
where mangoes were harvested
from just anywhere?

206
00:15:37,255 --> 00:15:39,085
That is not okay.

207
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:43,512
There's no mango
sweeter than Guimaras mangoes.

208
00:15:43,512 --> 00:15:48,649
And I was very clear that
what I want is Guimaras mango!

209
00:15:48,649 --> 00:15:51,749
Do you think I'll eat that
when you settled for less?

210
00:17:08,662 --> 00:17:10,148
Are you okay?

211
00:17:35,267 --> 00:17:36,752
Don't be shy.

212
00:17:38,803 --> 00:17:43,679
A philosopher once said,
"crying makes us human".

213
00:17:46,244 --> 00:17:47,630
Philosopher?

214
00:17:48,635 --> 00:17:50,274
Which philosopher?

215
00:17:51,209 --> 00:17:52,670
Me.

216
00:17:56,843 --> 00:18:00,080
So, you're the philosopher among them.

217
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:02,233
I'm just trying to make you laugh.

218
00:18:07,903 --> 00:18:09,408
Thank you.

219
00:18:11,093 --> 00:18:15,097
I guess you're aware that
they're just playing with you.

220
00:18:16,263 --> 00:18:18,899
I know that.

221
00:18:18,899 --> 00:18:22,836
I can feel that they're challenging me.

222
00:18:22,836 --> 00:18:27,650
But what can I do when I'm really your cook?

223
00:18:28,976 --> 00:18:34,744
I was clearly instructed
that you, guys, are my priority.

224
00:18:34,744 --> 00:18:39,359
So, whatever you want to eat,
no matter how difficult it is to cook,

225
00:18:39,359 --> 00:18:41,621
I need to find a way.

226
00:18:41,621 --> 00:18:43,096
I'm sorry.

227
00:18:44,691 --> 00:18:48,762
You keep saying sorry
when there's nothing to be sorry about.

228
00:18:48,762 --> 00:18:52,298
You only asked me to cook a scrambled egg.

229
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:55,544
To be fair, the scrambled eggs were perfect.

230
00:18:56,313 --> 00:18:58,188
Really?

231
00:18:58,188 --> 00:19:01,975
It looks like you're just saying it
to make me feel better.

232
00:19:01,975 --> 00:19:05,779
Well, yes, I'm trying to cheer you up,

233
00:19:05,779 --> 00:19:11,279
but it doesn't change the fact
that my scrambled eggs were delicious.

234
00:19:11,279 --> 00:19:14,582
Tomorrow, I want it sunny side up.

235
00:19:15,297 --> 00:19:17,960
So you're fond of eggs.

236
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:20,627
Just take it easy,
it might turn you into a chicken.

237
00:19:21,890 --> 00:19:23,259
Good one.

238
00:19:27,237 --> 00:19:29,503
Thank you.

239
00:19:29,503 --> 00:19:33,149
I needed a pep talk from
the philosopher of the Ferells.

240
00:19:34,474 --> 00:19:38,976
But don't worry,
tomorrow, I'll be okay again.

241
00:19:38,976 --> 00:19:42,062
I, out of all people, won't give up.

242
00:19:43,988 --> 00:19:45,552
You're brave.

243
00:19:57,264 --> 00:19:59,433
Did you see her earlier?

244
00:19:59,433 --> 00:20:01,535
She was so pitiful, Bro.

245
00:20:01,535 --> 00:20:03,437
I think she's not the brightest.

246
00:20:03,437 --> 00:20:06,073
Imagine, she looked for Guimaras mangoes

247
00:20:06,073 --> 00:20:08,275
for my mango pie here in Levante.

248
00:20:08,275 --> 00:20:09,976
I saw her when I passed by the kitchen,

249
00:20:09,976 --> 00:20:12,446
she was basically watching UTobe
on how to make sushi.

250
00:20:12,446 --> 00:20:13,747
Can you believe that?

251
00:20:13,747 --> 00:20:15,449
It's such a laugh trip.

252
00:20:15,449 --> 00:20:17,150
I'm having so much fun.

253
00:20:17,150 --> 00:20:18,351
Let's do it again tomorrow.

254
00:20:18,351 --> 00:20:20,020
Let's look for a more difficult food,

255
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:22,189
and then let's watch her
make a fool of herself.

256
00:20:22,189 --> 00:20:23,390
Game!

257
00:20:23,390 --> 00:20:27,186
Think about it, Guimaras mangoes in Levante?

258
00:20:29,396 --> 00:20:33,169
Do you think what you're doing is funny?

259
00:20:34,234 --> 00:20:35,819
What do you care?

260
00:20:38,205 --> 00:20:40,051
We're just having fun.

261
00:20:47,881 --> 00:20:49,049
I already spoke to the doctor.

262
00:20:49,049 --> 00:20:53,086
I told him it's better if I'll recover at home,

263
00:20:53,086 --> 00:20:54,521
so don't worry, my child.

264
00:20:54,521 --> 00:20:57,023
By tomorrow or the day after,
your father will be strong again.

265
00:20:57,023 --> 00:20:59,587
Stronger than a horse or carabao.

266
00:20:59,587 --> 00:21:04,030
That's good news, Father,
but don't force yourself.

267
00:21:04,030 --> 00:21:06,333
Just take it easy.

268
00:21:06,333 --> 00:21:09,136
You might go into a relapse
and have complications.

269
00:21:09,136 --> 00:21:13,332
Don't worry, Florence,
I'll take care of your father.

270
00:21:13,332 --> 00:21:18,011
I'll beat him up
if he skips his therapy and medicines.

271
00:21:18,011 --> 00:21:19,763
<i>It looks like it's more dangerous for me</i>

272
00:21:19,763 --> 00:21:21,516
<i>to get beaten up than have a relapse.</i>

273
00:21:22,716 --> 00:21:25,719
How about you, Florence?
How are you doing there?

274
00:21:25,719 --> 00:21:27,220
<i>Both of you...</i>

275
00:21:27,220 --> 00:21:31,124
You and your mother decided
without consulting me.

276
00:21:31,124 --> 00:21:33,693
Father, of course,
Mother and I don't want you to worry

277
00:21:33,693 --> 00:21:37,264
especially since you
were about to undergo surgery.

278
00:21:37,264 --> 00:21:39,366
Don't worry, Florence.

279
00:21:39,366 --> 00:21:41,101
I already explained it to your father.

280
00:21:41,101 --> 00:21:43,469
He's just being dramatic.

281
00:21:43,469 --> 00:21:46,431
<i>I understood your decision, my child.</i>

282
00:21:46,431 --> 00:21:50,877
You're sacrificing for me and our family,

283
00:21:50,877 --> 00:21:53,798
but of course, I'm still concerned about you.

284
00:21:55,682 --> 00:21:59,219
Well, are you doing okay there, Florence?

285
00:21:59,219 --> 00:22:00,954
<i>You don't have a problem?</i>

286
00:22:00,954 --> 00:22:02,389
Of course, Mother.

287
00:22:02,389 --> 00:22:04,224
There's no problem.

288
00:22:04,224 --> 00:22:06,193
I'm okay here.

289
00:22:06,193 --> 00:22:09,549
I might get used to this
and decide to live here.

290
00:22:09,549 --> 00:22:11,131
Oh, really?

291
00:22:11,131 --> 00:22:12,265
Are you sure, Florence?

292
00:22:12,265 --> 00:22:16,391
Remember, you made a promise to me
that the moment you get tired there,

293
00:22:16,391 --> 00:22:19,239
you'll come home here.

294
00:22:19,239 --> 00:22:20,574
<i>Think of yourself.</i>

295
00:22:20,574 --> 00:22:22,142
<i>Don't endure the pain.</i>

296
00:22:22,142 --> 00:22:24,945
Mother, I'm not suffering here.

297
00:22:24,945 --> 00:22:28,581
Well, I admit that I'm having a hard time

298
00:22:28,581 --> 00:22:32,251
because it's difficult to cook
for Don Ferell's grandsons,

299
00:22:32,251 --> 00:22:38,064
but I've been warned before
that they are very picky eaters.

300
00:22:38,064 --> 00:22:39,803
Kids are really like that, Florence.

301
00:22:39,803 --> 00:22:42,762
If the kids refuse to eat
what you've cooked for them,

302
00:22:42,762 --> 00:22:44,297
pinch them in the groin

303
00:22:44,297 --> 00:22:47,133
<i>or hit them a little on the head.</i>

304
00:22:48,134 --> 00:22:49,236
Hey, you're something else.

305
00:22:49,236 --> 00:22:51,004
Look at the advice you're giving
to your daughter.

306
00:22:51,004 --> 00:22:53,440
Don Ferell might get mad once he finds out

307
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:55,542
that she's hurting his grandsons.

308
00:22:55,542 --> 00:22:58,078
But, Florence, this is what I want to know.

309
00:22:58,078 --> 00:23:01,781
How are the people in the mansion?

310
00:23:01,781 --> 00:23:07,554
Are rich families normal like us?

311
00:23:07,554 --> 00:23:11,698
Or do they produce gold and magic?

312
00:23:15,395 --> 00:23:22,068
They're just like us,
but there's a difference.

313
00:23:22,068 --> 00:23:25,637
Actually, there's a big difference.

314
00:23:26,373 --> 00:23:28,300
What do you mean?

315
00:23:29,042 --> 00:23:31,278
Here in the world of rich people,

316
00:23:31,278 --> 00:23:34,180
it's quieter and no one is talking.

317
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:38,847
When you're here,
you won't hear any noise or conversations.

318
00:23:42,822 --> 00:23:44,962
<i>No one is talking.</i>

319
00:23:46,993 --> 00:23:49,796
<i>All of them have their own world.</i>

320
00:23:49,796 --> 00:23:52,299
<i>Compared to our place,
we can hear everything.</i>

321
00:23:52,299 --> 00:23:55,468
<i>The movement of the cats,
barking of the dogs,</i>

322
00:23:55,468 --> 00:23:59,172
<i>and even the rat's rustle,
we can hear it, right?</i>

323
00:23:59,172 --> 00:24:01,731
<i>If the silence in our place is deafening,</i>

324
00:24:01,731 --> 00:24:05,145
<i>we can hear the gossip-mongers the whole day.</i>

325
00:24:05,145 --> 00:24:10,110
<i>But here in the mansion,
the silence is deafening.</i>

326
00:24:13,386 --> 00:24:16,790
<i>It seems like it's so lonely there.</i>

327
00:24:16,790 --> 00:24:21,227
What's the use of being rich
if you don't talk to each other?

328
00:24:21,227 --> 00:24:23,563
If they're busy with their own worlds,

329
00:24:23,563 --> 00:24:26,433
how would they know
what's inside their hearts?

330
00:24:26,433 --> 00:24:29,703
I don't know, Father, but what I know is,

331
00:24:29,703 --> 00:24:34,107
I'll never exchange our simple life
for this mansion.

332
00:24:34,107 --> 00:24:37,086
Don't worry, Florence, you're already there.

333
00:24:37,086 --> 00:24:38,100
That's right.

334
00:24:38,100 --> 00:24:42,816
It's you who will bring noise,
fun, and light to that mansion.

335
00:24:42,816 --> 00:24:45,518
I hope so, Mother and Father.

336
00:24:45,518 --> 00:24:49,422
I hope I can share somehow
the happiness in our house

337
00:24:49,422 --> 00:24:55,523
so the people here can be happy
and somehow feel joy.

338
00:24:58,164 --> 00:24:59,499
I'll go ahead, Mother.

339
00:24:59,499 --> 00:25:01,265
And Father, get well soon and take it easy,

340
00:25:01,265 --> 00:25:03,136
<i>so you won't have a relapse.</i>

341
00:25:03,136 --> 00:25:04,170
Good night.

342
00:25:04,170 --> 00:25:06,973
I love you and I miss you.

343
00:25:06,973 --> 00:25:08,808
Good night, my child.

344
00:25:08,808 --> 00:25:10,828
I love you.

345
00:25:43,009 --> 00:25:45,178
Do you think I'm scared of you?

346
00:25:45,178 --> 00:25:47,731
I'm not scared of the Ferell brothers,

347
00:25:47,731 --> 00:25:50,524
and I don't care no matter who you are.

348
00:25:50,524 --> 00:25:51,751
Is that so?

349
00:25:51,751 --> 00:25:55,221
Project eliminate Florence Dela Cruz
activated.

350
00:25:55,221 --> 00:25:56,607
Let's go.

351
00:25:57,571 --> 00:25:59,426
Hey, get your hands off me!

352
00:25:59,426 --> 00:26:03,029
Ouch. What are you doing? Let me go!

353
00:26:10,570 --> 00:26:12,305
Thank you, Owen.

354
00:26:12,305 --> 00:26:17,812
Thank you for saving me
and choosing me over your brothers.

355
00:26:19,900 --> 00:26:22,635
I'll always be here for you, Florence.

356
00:26:53,480 --> 00:26:56,848
A new day, a new challenge.

357
00:26:56,848 --> 00:26:58,985
Can you still take it, Florence?

358
00:26:58,985 --> 00:27:02,798
Can you still cook for the naughty grandsons
of Grandpa Garp?

359
00:27:03,495 --> 00:27:06,912
Or you will follow what you promised
to Mother and Father

360
00:27:06,912 --> 00:27:08,729
and just go home?

361
00:27:14,875 --> 00:27:18,104
Can you give me a sign?

362
00:27:18,104 --> 00:27:21,783
Should I stay or should I go?

363
00:27:42,264 --> 00:27:47,166
Hey you, I thought a ghost is scaring me,
but it's just you.

364
00:27:47,166 --> 00:27:49,536
You frightened me.

365
00:27:49,536 --> 00:27:52,472
Have you been here for a while?

366
00:27:52,472 --> 00:27:54,507
I think you got lost.

367
00:27:54,507 --> 00:27:56,061
Where did you come from?

368
00:28:13,593 --> 00:28:18,249
Never ever give up, you can do it.

369
00:28:32,312 --> 00:28:33,613
Hi.

370
00:28:33,613 --> 00:28:35,287
Here it is.

371
00:28:39,492 --> 00:28:42,689
So, how was it, Mr. Dencio?

372
00:28:43,679 --> 00:28:45,358
You know,

373
00:28:45,358 --> 00:28:50,016
this paella negra of yours is more delicious
if there's a vermouth.

374
00:28:51,831 --> 00:28:53,316
Vermouth?

375
00:28:54,334 --> 00:28:56,122
A Spanish wine.

376
00:28:58,938 --> 00:29:01,007
As a matter of fact,

377
00:29:01,007 --> 00:29:06,545
vermouth came from France and Italy,

378
00:29:06,545 --> 00:29:09,949
but it became famous in Spain.

379
00:29:09,949 --> 00:29:12,318
Shall I hit you with this?

380
00:29:12,318 --> 00:29:16,793
Wait, how come you know a lot about food?

381
00:29:16,793 --> 00:29:20,702
That's because, with all the food
the different chefs have cooked

382
00:29:20,702 --> 00:29:22,829
and rejected by the Ferell brothers,

383
00:29:22,829 --> 00:29:28,301
we somehow got used to sophisticated food.

384
00:29:28,301 --> 00:29:29,535
That's true.

385
00:29:29,535 --> 00:29:33,410
As for me,
my favorite is the classic French meal,

386
00:29:33,410 --> 00:29:37,909
Coq au vin, a delicious chicken stew.

387
00:29:37,909 --> 00:29:40,446
I remember that.

388
00:29:40,446 --> 00:29:43,710
Of course, you can't outvote my favorite,

389
00:29:43,710 --> 00:29:51,067
tomato bruschetta with balsamico
di moderna from the Italian cuisine.

390
00:29:51,067 --> 00:29:53,997
- Excuse me?
- Yes?

391
00:29:53,997 --> 00:29:57,330
It's not moderna, but modena.

392
00:29:57,330 --> 00:30:03,703
Balsamico di modena, fettucine, linguine!

393
00:30:03,703 --> 00:30:05,972
Lamborghini, Ferrari...

394
00:30:05,972 --> 00:30:08,507
Confetti!

395
00:30:09,142 --> 00:30:14,914
And you, don't feel bad
because you can cook delicious food.

396
00:30:14,914 --> 00:30:16,249
Is that right? Right?

397
00:30:16,249 --> 00:30:18,751
- Yes.
- Yes!

398
00:30:18,751 --> 00:30:22,988
It just so happens that my wards
are picky eaters.

399
00:30:23,823 --> 00:30:27,660
Don't worry, Florence, we're just here.

400
00:30:27,660 --> 00:30:31,497
We're ready to eat the food
they refuse to eat.

401
00:30:33,332 --> 00:30:37,783
But, Mr. Dencio, may I just ask,

402
00:30:37,783 --> 00:30:40,862
why are the Ferells like that
when it comes to food?

403
00:30:41,917 --> 00:30:44,877
I have no idea, Florence.

404
00:30:44,877 --> 00:30:46,779
But from what I heard,

405
00:30:46,779 --> 00:30:54,553
the late wife of Don Ferell, Dona Amanda,
was a very good cook.

406
00:30:55,523 --> 00:30:57,057
That's true.

407
00:30:58,222 --> 00:31:01,160
My father who used to work here
for a long time in the mansion

408
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:04,263
told me that.

409
00:31:04,263 --> 00:31:09,368
And whenever Dona Amanda cooks,
it's like there's a feast.

410
00:31:09,368 --> 00:31:11,938
They all want to be together.

411
00:31:11,938 --> 00:31:16,042
Everyone is excited about
the food Dona Amanda cooked.

412
00:31:16,042 --> 00:31:21,013
No, Dona Amanda is very talented.

413
00:31:21,013 --> 00:31:23,582
According to Serafica...

414
00:31:25,885 --> 00:31:27,420
Just by the scent,

415
00:31:27,420 --> 00:31:32,592
Dona Amanda already knows
if her food is delicious or not.

416
00:31:32,592 --> 00:31:36,627
Too bad their children didn't inherit
the talent of Dona Amanda

417
00:31:36,627 --> 00:31:38,364
when it comes to cooking,

418
00:31:38,364 --> 00:31:42,664
but they became busy with
their respective businesses of the Ferells.

419
00:31:42,664 --> 00:31:46,064
That's why the grandsons
were left with Grandpa Garp.

420
00:31:47,874 --> 00:31:54,680
What hurts the most is,
when Dona Amanda died,

421
00:31:54,680 --> 00:31:58,350
it's like the system here
in the mansion changed.

422
00:31:59,018 --> 00:32:01,754
Before, it was happy.

423
00:32:02,789 --> 00:32:05,090
They ate together.

424
00:32:06,225 --> 00:32:12,360
But now, it looks like they are on their own.

425
00:32:14,515 --> 00:32:17,685
It's like they don't care about each other.

426
00:32:48,634 --> 00:32:51,493
Florence, do you know the saying,

427
00:32:51,493 --> 00:32:54,607
"the way to a man's heart
is through his stomach"?

428
00:32:54,607 --> 00:32:56,175
Yes.

429
00:32:56,175 --> 00:32:58,444
That saying is so worn out...

430
00:32:58,444 --> 00:33:03,115
It's more worn out compared to the saying,
"love is blind".

431
00:33:03,115 --> 00:33:07,406
Even if it's a worn-out saying,
there's still some truth to it.

432
00:33:07,406 --> 00:33:09,789
And besides,
your mother and I won't be a couple

433
00:33:09,789 --> 00:33:12,491
if not for this recipe.

434
00:33:12,491 --> 00:33:14,785
Father, what are you cooking?

435
00:33:14,785 --> 00:33:19,131
This is what you call, "a heart that loves".

436
00:33:32,645 --> 00:33:34,046
Okay, send that over to the office.

437
00:33:34,046 --> 00:33:35,304
Okay, Sir.

438
00:33:47,927 --> 00:33:49,406
Grandpa Garp?

439
00:33:51,297 --> 00:33:53,099
Can I talk to you?

440
00:33:53,099 --> 00:33:54,409
Yes, you can.

441
00:33:55,997 --> 00:34:01,408
I just want to ask why you hired me?

442
00:34:03,276 --> 00:34:09,015
I just want to find out
why you got me as your cook.

443
00:34:09,015 --> 00:34:14,665
I'm just a simple cook, I'm not a chef.

444
00:34:17,690 --> 00:34:21,394
I'm just my mother's assistant
in her mobile eatery.

445
00:34:21,394 --> 00:34:25,531
And I didn't also study
in any of the prestigious cooking schools.

446
00:34:25,531 --> 00:34:28,534
And I don't have any work experience

447
00:34:28,534 --> 00:34:31,270
in any of the sophisticated restaurants.

448
00:34:31,270 --> 00:34:35,941
I have no capability to cook whatever
your grandsons would like to eat,

449
00:34:35,941 --> 00:34:42,214
especially the dishes for the rich,
like international dishes.

450
00:34:42,214 --> 00:34:46,352
What I can only do is home cooked dishes.

451
00:34:46,352 --> 00:34:52,825
But despite that,
you still hired me as a cook here.

452
00:34:53,962 --> 00:34:58,667
Why did you even hire me
despite my limitations?

453
00:35:05,438 --> 00:35:07,139
I agree.

454
00:35:07,139 --> 00:35:11,944
The first time I saw you, it made me think,
"Serafica is going crazy".

455
00:35:11,944 --> 00:35:17,694
She's so desperate to hire someone like you.

456
00:35:17,694 --> 00:35:18,977
I will be honest with you.

457
00:35:18,977 --> 00:35:21,387
I didn't expect much,

458
00:35:21,387 --> 00:35:26,512
knowing that when it comes to food,
my grandsons are so picky.

459
00:35:26,512 --> 00:35:31,083
I didn't even expect that you'll stay long
in this household as a cook.

460
00:35:31,998 --> 00:35:35,968
But when I tasted your dish, the balbacua,

461
00:35:35,968 --> 00:35:37,931
I already told you, remember?

462
00:35:37,931 --> 00:35:41,193
I remembered my wife's cooking...

463
00:35:43,211 --> 00:35:44,285
What?

464
00:35:44,285 --> 00:35:47,072
You stir the salad, get it from the bottom,

465
00:35:47,072 --> 00:35:48,814
and the sauce should be on top.

466
00:35:48,814 --> 00:35:51,317
- This is about to be cooked.
- No, not yet!

467
00:35:51,317 --> 00:35:52,718
It smells good.

468
00:35:52,718 --> 00:35:55,988
You can't taste this yet, it's still raw.

469
00:35:55,988 --> 00:35:57,023
You're always hungry...

470
00:35:57,023 --> 00:35:58,891
Come over here. No, that's off-limits!

471
00:35:58,891 --> 00:36:00,620
Mix this.

472
00:36:00,620 --> 00:36:01,794
Hey, what now?

473
00:36:01,794 --> 00:36:05,164
Yes, that's correct,
and then put the carrots after that.

474
00:36:05,164 --> 00:36:07,105
Not too much water, son. There, very good.

475
00:36:07,105 --> 00:36:08,434
Hey, that's not yet cooked...

476
00:36:08,434 --> 00:36:10,102
Out, out, out!

477
00:36:13,739 --> 00:36:15,178
You, guys...

478
00:36:15,178 --> 00:36:18,877
Here, you really want this?

479
00:36:22,848 --> 00:36:28,104
Maybe I was hoping you can match my wife
when it comes to cooking.

480
00:36:29,289 --> 00:36:33,527
Her cooking was so good
it bonded us as a family.

481
00:36:33,527 --> 00:36:39,097
Every time we eat, we could feel that
we're a complete and happy family.

482
00:36:40,122 --> 00:36:44,459
I was hoping that you can
make us a happy family again.

483
00:36:46,381 --> 00:36:48,276
But you're right.

484
00:36:51,110 --> 00:36:53,412
I was being unfair.

485
00:36:53,412 --> 00:36:56,142
I expected too much of you.

486
00:36:57,646 --> 00:37:01,087
I hired you for the wrong reason,

487
00:37:01,087 --> 00:37:06,578
that's why, I'm apologizing to you.

488
00:37:08,194 --> 00:37:11,797
Now if you're really having a hard time
and you can't do it,

489
00:37:11,797 --> 00:37:14,200
I'll understand why you'd want to resign.

490
00:37:14,200 --> 00:37:16,035
- What?
- And for all your troubles,

491
00:37:16,035 --> 00:37:19,802
I'm willing to give you
a very good separation pay.

492
00:37:19,802 --> 00:37:23,226
No... No, I won't resign, Grandpa Garp.

493
00:37:24,076 --> 00:37:27,555
I can achieve your expectations of me.

494
00:37:27,555 --> 00:37:30,330
What I can't do is match
how good your wife is,

495
00:37:30,330 --> 00:37:32,918
when it comes to cooking.

496
00:37:32,918 --> 00:37:36,809
We have different styles of cooking, right?

497
00:37:36,809 --> 00:37:41,760
But I can help you become
a complete family again.

498
00:37:41,760 --> 00:37:47,653
Or at the very least,
eat together like a family.

499
00:37:47,653 --> 00:37:48,949
But...

500
00:37:51,058 --> 00:37:53,274
But what?

501
00:37:53,274 --> 00:37:58,812
But I need your help,
because I can't do this alone.

502
00:37:59,945 --> 00:38:02,172
Okay, what will I do?

503
00:38:10,551 --> 00:38:12,057
Hello.

504
00:38:12,057 --> 00:38:13,459
Nanny, this is Aldus.

505
00:38:13,459 --> 00:38:15,461
Yes, Aldus. Do you need anything?

506
00:38:15,461 --> 00:38:17,629
Is she dead already?

507
00:38:17,629 --> 00:38:19,429
<i>Or did she quit?</i>

508
00:38:19,429 --> 00:38:20,922
Who?

509
00:38:20,922 --> 00:38:22,868
Who else, but our cook?

510
00:38:22,868 --> 00:38:24,537
Of course, not.

511
00:38:24,537 --> 00:38:25,571
She's still here.

512
00:38:25,571 --> 00:38:28,674
She's probably busy making your lunch.

513
00:38:28,674 --> 00:38:29,808
Really?

514
00:38:29,808 --> 00:38:31,977
But how come she hasn't asked
for my order yet?

515
00:38:31,977 --> 00:38:34,947
Like I said, I want Italian for my lunch.

516
00:38:34,947 --> 00:38:36,415
Are you sure?

517
00:38:36,415 --> 00:38:39,251
She didn't ask you what you want for lunch?

518
00:38:39,251 --> 00:38:40,252
Yes, Ma'am.

519
00:38:40,252 --> 00:38:42,054
Actually, Florence is not yet here,

520
00:38:42,054 --> 00:38:44,123
and I haven't seen her since breakfast.

521
00:38:44,123 --> 00:38:45,354
So where is she?

522
00:38:45,354 --> 00:38:46,535
All right.

523
00:39:06,145 --> 00:39:07,926
What are you doing?

524
00:39:07,926 --> 00:39:10,816
I'm preparing for lunch.

525
00:39:10,816 --> 00:39:13,118
How come you only have one dish?

526
00:39:13,118 --> 00:39:17,356
Didn't I tell you that
they each have their own food?

527
00:39:17,356 --> 00:39:21,460
That is why you always have to cook them
their own unique meals

528
00:39:21,460 --> 00:39:23,760
because they have
their respective food preferences.

529
00:39:23,760 --> 00:39:25,954
What were you thinking, Florence?

530
00:39:25,954 --> 00:39:30,502
What came into your mind
to disobey my orders?

531
00:39:30,502 --> 00:39:32,705
I requested for this, Serafica.

532
00:39:32,705 --> 00:39:34,341
Don Ferell.

533
00:39:36,065 --> 00:39:39,356
Call the kids and tell them to join me
at the dining table.

534
00:39:39,356 --> 00:39:40,646
Yes, Sir.

535
00:39:40,646 --> 00:39:42,365
Right away, Sir.

536
00:39:56,061 --> 00:39:57,963
This is nice.

537
00:39:57,963 --> 00:40:00,986
Finally, we'll eat together.

538
00:40:02,568 --> 00:40:05,838
I can't remember the last time this happened,

539
00:40:05,838 --> 00:40:08,994
maybe because it's been a long time.

540
00:40:08,994 --> 00:40:15,046
Either that or maybe I can't remember,
because I'm becoming senile.

541
00:40:17,646 --> 00:40:19,985
Grandpa Garp, sorry to say this,

542
00:40:19,985 --> 00:40:24,939
but I already told Ms. Serafica
that I prefer Italian for my lunch.

543
00:40:24,939 --> 00:40:26,878
Actually, Grandpa, me too.

544
00:40:26,878 --> 00:40:29,962
I also want chicken teriyaki.

545
00:40:29,962 --> 00:40:33,824
Me too, Grandpa,
I'm craving for Chinese food.

546
00:40:33,824 --> 00:40:35,646
I was planning to order because I heard

547
00:40:35,646 --> 00:40:38,987
there's a newly opened
Cantonese style restaurant in the city.

548
00:40:40,530 --> 00:40:41,707
This looks nice, Grandpa.

549
00:40:41,707 --> 00:40:43,909
What did you prepare for us?

550
00:40:43,909 --> 00:40:49,881
Florence calls this
the soup of the loving heart.

551
00:40:49,881 --> 00:40:52,054
Cute! It's actually very witty, Grandpa,

552
00:40:52,054 --> 00:40:53,720
because if you look very close,

553
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:56,889
you can see it's a tamarind broth
with banana blossoms.

554
00:40:56,889 --> 00:41:00,120
It suits the name the loving heart.

555
00:41:00,120 --> 00:41:04,563
Just because that dish has a cute name,
you expect us to eat that, Owen?

556
00:41:04,563 --> 00:41:08,577
Honestly, I'm not in the mood
for another Filipino soup.

557
00:41:08,577 --> 00:41:12,386
Not to disrespect,
but it doesn't look appetizing.

558
00:41:14,970 --> 00:41:18,753
Does this have meat
or just full of banana hearts?

559
00:41:18,753 --> 00:41:20,472
Please...

560
00:41:22,119 --> 00:41:24,547
Let's give this a chance first.

561
00:41:24,547 --> 00:41:29,654
Now if you really don't like it,
I will fire Florence.

562
00:41:29,654 --> 00:41:34,954
But taste it first,
so you'd know if you'll like it or not.

563
00:41:44,317 --> 00:41:46,745
Grandpa Gard is right.

564
00:41:46,745 --> 00:41:49,508
As for me, it's okay,
and my life's motto anyway,

565
00:41:49,508 --> 00:41:52,811
is I try everything at least once.

566
00:41:56,148 --> 00:41:57,908
Okay, let's eat.

567
00:42:00,319 --> 00:42:01,730
Go ahead and eat.

568
00:42:08,754 --> 00:42:10,734
What's happening?

569
00:42:10,734 --> 00:42:12,583
Tell me, Florence.

570
00:42:12,583 --> 00:42:14,646
Why is this happening?

571
00:42:15,770 --> 00:42:19,015
I thought of talking to Grandpa Garp.

572
00:42:20,143 --> 00:42:25,219
Did you talk to Don Ferell
without asking my permission?

573
00:42:27,296 --> 00:42:28,956
What's with you?

574
00:42:28,956 --> 00:42:33,285
Are you compromising
my position in this family?

575
00:42:37,494 --> 00:42:39,925
Let me explain Ms. Serafica.

576
00:42:39,925 --> 00:42:46,165
I thought of a way
how I can do my job better as a cook here.

577
00:42:46,165 --> 00:42:47,982
Go on.

578
00:42:47,982 --> 00:42:50,039
I thought that

579
00:42:50,039 --> 00:42:54,766
even if I watch videos from UTobe
the whole day

580
00:42:54,766 --> 00:42:57,843
on how to cook Spanish, French,
or Italian dishes,

581
00:42:57,843 --> 00:43:02,987
or whatever country that is,
I will not learn that.

582
00:43:02,987 --> 00:43:05,298
That's why, I told Grandpa Garp

583
00:43:05,298 --> 00:43:09,222
if he hired me
to cook whatever his grandsons like,

584
00:43:09,222 --> 00:43:11,456
he made the wrong decision.

585
00:43:12,355 --> 00:43:15,160
You said what?

586
00:43:15,160 --> 00:43:17,496
That's the thing, Ms. Serafica.

587
00:43:17,496 --> 00:43:20,332
I told him that what I can only cook

588
00:43:20,332 --> 00:43:23,668
is what I've learned
from my parent's kitchen.

589
00:43:23,668 --> 00:43:28,115
I can only cook the kinds of food
that I cook for my family.

590
00:43:28,115 --> 00:43:30,036
If he doesn't want that,

591
00:43:30,036 --> 00:43:33,330
I do not deserve to be the cook
for his grandsons.

592
00:43:35,347 --> 00:43:37,751
So you took the initiative?

593
00:43:39,496 --> 00:43:45,537
Well, next time inform me first
before you talk to Don Ferell.

594
00:43:45,537 --> 00:43:47,165
Is that clear?

595
00:43:51,430 --> 00:43:55,147
But I admire your courage.

596
00:43:57,269 --> 00:43:58,370
Owen.

597
00:43:58,370 --> 00:44:00,036
Florence?

598
00:44:00,036 --> 00:44:01,139
Owen.

599
00:44:01,139 --> 00:44:02,497
Can we talk?

600
00:44:02,497 --> 00:44:04,059
Sure.

601
00:44:04,059 --> 00:44:05,210
You're awesome.

602
00:44:05,210 --> 00:44:07,022
You're really good.

603
00:44:07,022 --> 00:44:09,131
I'm impressed with you.

604
00:44:10,850 --> 00:44:13,070
Wait, what's happening?

605
00:44:13,070 --> 00:44:15,186
Everyone appreciated your cooking.

606
00:44:15,186 --> 00:44:16,587
Really?

607
00:44:16,587 --> 00:44:17,588
How?

608
00:44:17,588 --> 00:44:20,258
Earlier, Grandpa Garp challenged us.

609
00:44:20,258 --> 00:44:21,292
He said...

610
00:44:21,292 --> 00:44:22,794
<i>Taste it first.</i>

611
00:44:22,794 --> 00:44:27,309
Now if you really don't like it,
I will fire Florence.

612
00:44:27,309 --> 00:44:30,088
And if anyone of us doesn't like your food,

613
00:44:30,088 --> 00:44:32,036
we'll just tell him and he'll fire you.

614
00:44:32,036 --> 00:44:34,972
- Decision?
- Exactly.

615
00:44:34,972 --> 00:44:37,075
So am I fired already?

616
00:44:37,075 --> 00:44:38,376
I'll go pack my things,

617
00:44:38,376 --> 00:44:41,723
because it's impossible
that you all liked my cooking.

618
00:44:41,723 --> 00:44:45,183
That's the thing
because all of us liked your cooking.

619
00:44:45,183 --> 00:44:47,518
- It's impossible.
- Yes.

620
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:49,220
As in, everyone?

621
00:44:49,220 --> 00:44:50,381
Yes.

622
00:44:50,381 --> 00:44:52,423
As in, all of you?

623
00:44:52,423 --> 00:44:53,486
Yes.

624
00:44:53,486 --> 00:44:55,330
Including Tristan?

625
00:44:56,092 --> 00:44:58,064
Troy?

626
00:44:58,064 --> 00:44:59,860
Aldus?

627
00:44:59,860 --> 00:45:01,065
And even Nero?

628
00:45:01,065 --> 00:45:03,045
Yes, including Nero.

629
00:45:03,045 --> 00:45:05,536
- Wow.
- Not only that.

630
00:45:05,536 --> 00:45:07,472
Grandpa decided that from now on,

631
00:45:07,472 --> 00:45:10,278
you'll decide what we're going to eat.

632
00:45:11,066 --> 00:45:12,510
Really?

633
00:45:12,510 --> 00:45:14,034
Promise.

634
00:45:49,727 --> 00:45:53,554
I'm happy that I met you.

635
00:45:53,554 --> 00:45:57,507
I'm happy too,
that I'll always taste your loving heart.

636
00:46:13,002 --> 00:46:14,939
It's you again?

637
00:46:14,939 --> 00:46:17,259
You even woke me up.

638
00:46:30,021 --> 00:46:32,433
Don't get tired of dreaming.

639
00:46:49,952 --> 00:46:51,696
Grandpa Garp, I'm sorry.

640
00:46:51,696 --> 00:46:53,454
I have a proposal for you.

641
00:46:53,454 --> 00:46:55,094
You can still cook for us,

642
00:46:55,094 --> 00:47:00,604
but now you have the option to study at GU,
if you want?

643
00:47:00,604 --> 00:47:04,107
Can you balance work and study
at the same time?

644
00:47:04,107 --> 00:47:05,957
Won't you have a hard time?

645
00:47:05,957 --> 00:47:09,227
No, don't worry. I can handle that.

646
00:47:09,227 --> 00:47:10,428
Me, of all people.

647
00:47:10,428 --> 00:47:11,200
Owen?

648
00:47:11,200 --> 00:47:12,857
Nero is okay with you.

649
00:47:12,857 --> 00:47:14,834
You think he's just mad,
but he's okay with you.

650
00:47:14,834 --> 00:47:16,367
As a matter of fact,

651
00:47:16,367 --> 00:47:18,736
he's one of your biggest defenders
here in the mansion.

652
00:47:18,736 --> 00:47:20,604
How did that happen?

653
00:47:21,289 --> 00:47:22,617
Nero?

654
00:47:23,613 --> 00:47:24,875
He's early.

655
00:47:24,875 --> 00:47:26,660
Where is he going?

656
00:47:29,385 --> 00:47:31,087
How are you doing?
